e with every order this makes a  perfect last minute gift for somebody a  loved one or a friend and established  titles is actually running a big labor  day sale right now plus if you use the  code cosmic wonder you get an additional  10 off so go to establishtitles.com  cosmic wonder to get your gifts now and  help support the channel and establish  titles told me that the first 200 people  purchasing a title pack using my link  will effectively be next to my plot  within a few minutes of walking distance  depending on how many of you want to  become a lord or a lady we can build our  own little cosmic wonder kingdom now  disney's d23 expo is coming up in about  a week now and of course we're all super  hyped for it because there's the  possibility that they could be revealing  some projects that revolve around the  mutants and while i definitely think  that they need to introduce at least  some mutants before secret wars i think  the mutants are really going to be  coming after secret wars in fact i think  the entire next saga phase 7 phase 8  phase 9 is going to be the mutants saga  i called that in a previous video but  i'm calling it again right now and if  marvel is going to do what i think  they're about to do the avengers kind of  won't be prominent figures in the mcu  anymore but it's really going to be all  about the x-men and the fantastic four  now the infinity saga was awesome it was  the best it was fantastic and the  multiversal saga is going pretty well  some people have some issues with it but  we've gotten a lot of great projects  from it and of course we still have  phase 5 and phase 6 to play out before  this saga is over but before this saga  ends i think it's going to set up the  groundwork for the next phase obviously  and i think that they're going to do  that with the x-men because they're  going to build the x-men team and i'm  assuming that they're going to do that  much like they did the avengers team and  this is where it kind of resets because  i think marvel and kevin feige actually  wants to build the x-men much like they  did the avengers team in the beginning  and what i mean by that is have  individual solo movies that kind of  connect with other movies until they  eventually all have to come together to  fight some big great cause and when i  think about this i think it makes the  most sense and i actually think it could  be one of the most exciting ways to do  it especially since we know that kevin  feige doesn't like to do things the way  things have been done before a perfect  example of this is spider-man when  captain america civil war introduced  spider-man we did not get really a  traditional origin story they didn't  dive into it too much but we didn't get  the uncle ben story we thought we were  going to get it in spider-man homecoming  but we still didn't and honestly we  never really got anything about uncle  ben in the spider-man homecoming trilogy  except for the briefcase that had his  initials on it but basically aunt may  was our uncle ben of the spider-man  homecoming trilogy that is a perfect  example of kevin feige kind of wanting  to do things a little bit differently  and i think that will remain true for  the x-men especially since kevin feige  himself worked on the x-men films the  original ones at least now the x-men  have kind of been done in two different  ways so far the first way that was done  in the first x-men movie that we got was  that the x-men team was already  established then we went to the newer  x-men movies where we got the backstory  of magneto and professor xavier we watch  them come together and then we watch  them form the x-men team then of course  we watch magneto break away with half of  the mutants now since kevin feige is  most likely going to want to do things a  little bit differently i think that it's  going to be a combination of the two and  i think this is how phase seven is going  to start off i think that in the end of  phase six and in secret wars we'll get a  big setup for the x-men so the team will  kind of be established but then in phase  seven we'll start with our individual  movies i think there will be a  relatively small x-men team established  in the mcu i think most of the x-men  that we might get in secret wars could  be variants could be from other  universes possibly the fox universe a  recent rumor going around is that when  deadpool enters the mcu he is going to  bring some of the fox x-men with him and  they will have somewhat of a role to  play in secret wars that would establish  the x-men team that would show us hey  the x-men do exist and it would tell the  people in our universe hey they probably  exist somewhere here as well so phase 7  could start with individual films like a  cyclops film like a rogue film they  could possibly do a wolverine solo film  however i think they might stay away  from that for a little bit but i think  during this time we're going to see  professor x recruit x-men i think  professor x is going to have already  established somewhat of an x-men team  over at the x-men mansion and at the  start of phase 7 we'll start to see the  recruitment process and the way marvel  studios has set this up is actually  quite clever what they did in miss  marvel sets up the individual films in  the future they essentially established  that some people have the ex-gene  however they need something to awaken it  this was the bangle for kamala khan it  also seems like they're kind of  retconning the scarlet witch to actually  be a mutant although she is a powerful  witch she could also have the mutant  gene that was activated by the infinity  stone so some of the x-men could already  exist and their mutant powers already be  activated but we could also see new  mutants powers get activated and these  could be our solo films until eventually  they come together for a big x-men film  much like the avengers came together for  the first avengers film now from here on  out it's going to get pretty cool  because they're not just going to  completely get rid of all of the other  characters that existed before phase 7.  so we'll still have the scarlet witch  there some of the avengers are still  going to be there hopefully spider-man  is still going to be there but the  fantastic four are also going to be  coming into the picture as well so  they're going to be blended in with the  x-men 2. and i believe that these two  groups are sort of going to be the main  focus of the mcu moving forward starting  with phase 7. until eventually we have a  huge movie like avengers infinity war  that brings not only the x-men and the  fantastic four together but of course  also the avengers together and the new  guardians team as well basically this is  how i think it's going to go down phase  7 starts off with some individual mutant  projects then we're going to get another  fantastic four film that could be in  phase 8 depending on what their timeline  is also during phase 7 we will get our  other little projects as well that'll  kind of show us the side stories of some  new avengers possibly the young avengers  and some of the new characters that are  being introduced then i think we'll be  getting our first official x-men film  after that they'll continue to do  individual x-men movies but we'll start  to see the actual x-men group interact  with people like reed richards in the  fantastic four and also of course the  avengers now these will be brief  interactions and we may see some movies  and some projects where we see a couple  members of different teams interact with  each other but not the full full-on  teams interacting and fighting with each  other to try to save earth or the  universe as a whole basically it has to  build you can't just throw everyone  together all at once then there's no  climax there's nothing exciting left to  see so that's why i think marvel studios  has to start off with these individual  mutant projects build them up into the  first x-men team then continue  recruiting and introducing new x-men  members all the while having them  interact with some members of the  avengers and the fantastic four until  eventually i think all of them are going  to have to come together to fight  galactus if we're talking about big bads  the one that's on the table that's  probably not going to be used in the  multiversal saga is galactus and what  better villain to bring together the  x-men the fantastic four and the  avengers so i really think that after  phase six phase seven is going to kick  off another amazing saga which again i  believe is going to be the mutant saga  that will focus on the mutants and the  fantastic four but of course have the  avengers there as well and to end this  saga we'll see all of the teams come  together and honestly if this happens  even remotely close to how i think it's  going to happen it'll probably be the  best saga marvel had to focus on the  avengers for years and years and years  because they didn't have the rights to  the x-men or the fantastic four but now  that they do they can kind of switch the  focus and give the avengers a little bit  of a break so the shift of the main  focus of the mcu would go from the  avengers to the x-men and the fantastic  four and i think that this is going to  make a heck of a saga but let me know  your thoughts about this in the comments  down below please don't forget to like  the video and subscribe to stay up to  date on all things relating to the mcu  for live updates you can follow me on  instagram and twitter and as always  thank you all so much for watching woof

